---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'who-we-share-with', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children and school learners' },
  { id: 'how-long', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'How we protect it' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', title: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
];
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  slug="privacy"
  description="How The Consultant collects, uses and protects the information you share through this website, our forms and WhatsApp."
  lead="What we collect when you contact us or apply for training, why we need it, and how to see, correct or delete it."
  updated="2026-09-25"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      The Consultant ("we", "us") is a technology consulting, software development and training firm based in Ghana. We
      are responsible for the personal data described in this policy, and we handle it in line with Ghana's{' '}
      <strong>Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843)</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions about your data go to <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a> or {site.phones[0].display}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-we-collect">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>When you send a message</h3>
    <p>Your name, your phone number and/or email, what you need help with, and your message.</p>
    <h3>When you apply for training</h3>
    <p>
      The learner's name, level (JHS, SHS or university), class or year and gender; a phone number, and optionally an
      email and the country you are in; for JHS and SHS learners, a parent or guardian's name and phone number; and
      the program, start month, duration, mode of training and any note you add.
    </p>
    <h3>When you call, email or WhatsApp us</h3>
    <p>Your number or address and whatever you choose to tell us in the conversation.</p>
    <h3>Collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      To stop spam and abuse of our forms, our server records a <strong>one-way hashed</strong> version of your IP
      address when you send a message. It cannot be turned back into your address. Our server logs record errors and
      timings, never the contents of the forms. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use-it">
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss your project.</li>
      <li>To process a training application: confirm the class, schedule and fees, and keep in touch while you train.</li>
      <li>To contact a parent or guardian about a school learner's training.</li>
      <li>To keep our forms safe from spam and misuse.</li>
      <li>To meet our legal and accounting obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use your details because you asked us to (to answer you or enrol you), and for the ordinary running of our
      business. We <strong>do not sell</strong> personal data, and we do not send marketing messages unless you have
      agreed to receive them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="who-we-share-with">
    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We only share data with the services that run this website and our forms, and only what each one needs:</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Service</th><th>What it does for us</th><th>What it receives</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosts the website and stores contact messages</td><td>Contact form details, hashed IP</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google (Forms &amp; Sheets)</td><td>Receives and stores training applications</td><td>Everything in the application form</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Emails our team when a new message arrives</td><td>The message and your contact details</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WhatsApp (Meta)</td><td>Chats you start with us</td><td>What you send in the chat</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Some of these providers process data on servers outside Ghana. We choose providers with strong security and privacy
      commitments. We may also disclose data where the law requires it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>Children and school learners</h2>
    <p>
      We train JHS and SHS learners, many of whom are under 18. For these learners we ask for a parent or guardian's
      name and phone number, and we may contact them to confirm the application, fees and schedule. A parent or
      guardian can ask to see, correct or delete their child's data at any time using the contact details above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-long">
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep enquiries and applications for up to <strong>24 months</strong> after our last contact with you, then
      delete them. If you enrol or become a client, we keep the records we need to run your course or project, and
      what the law requires us to keep for tax and accounting, for as long as those purposes apply.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served only over encrypted connections (HTTPS). Access to stored messages and applications is limited
      to our team and protected by sign-in. No system is perfectly secure, but if a breach ever affected your data we
      would tell you and the Data Protection Commission as the law requires.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights">
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the Data Protection Act, you can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you what data we hold about you and give you a copy;</li>
      <li>correct anything that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
      <li>delete your data, or stop using it for a particular purpose.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>. We may need to confirm who you are first, and we will respond as quickly as we
      can. If you are unhappy with how we handled your data, you can complain to Ghana's{' '}
      <a href="https://dataprotection.org.gh" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Data Protection Commission</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use advertising, analytics or tracking cookies, so there is nothing to accept or decline.
      A sign-in cookie is used only by our staff on the private admin area. When you open WhatsApp or Google Forms from
      our site, those services apply their own privacy and cookie policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how we handle personal data, we will update this page and the "Last updated" date above.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
